 "note": "Characters track CH-5: the figure kit's shapes as data (game/js/logic/figure-kit.js builds everyone's figure from their look with these; logic/kit-shapes.js reads the shape lists). heads: each head shape's knobs (r: its radii as parts of the usual head's; jaw: how V, below 0 wider at the jaw; chin: how far it drops; cheek: the cheekbones; crown: the back of the skull; face: how flat; nose: a fixed nose, 0 button, 1 straight, 2 long, 3 broad, else each person's own); hero is the main character's and never picked at random. vary: how far each person strays from their head shape ([base, spread] times a number from their seed). builds: multipliers on the look's sliders (k), how each walks (gait), and how much more V its jaw (jaw). folk: the builds townsfolk are picked from. proportions: chibi (head, legs, torso, arms, neck) and sliderGain (how much more a slider counts on a figure). hair: each style's recipe: cut (the hairline: front, side, back), thin (a close cap), under (what shows under a hat: len [min, max] metres at the usual head, w, strand, lift; tail), and steps (grow, spikes, bun, tie, twin) with their strands' numbers (grav, stiff, wave, freq, curl, hug). accessories: each wardrobe id's shapes: vars (named values, in order), and rows: id, parent part, at, shape (a primitive of logic/figure-pose.js, or dome, disc, lathe, band and curls round the head), col (a colour slot); sides makes an A and a B mirrored (s is 1 then -1), repeat n makes id0..id(n-1) (i); a value is a number or a sum like 'bx * 0.98' of the frame's values (a hat's: k, rx, yb, zc, bx, bz, top; the head's: k, hx, hy, c1; the body's: tk, girth, hipK, torsoZ) with sqrt, sin, cos and pi. fringe: a fringe shows under this hat. colour: the slot's own colour over the item's.",
